module gunbc.recurring_failure_mode.a_dispatch_surface_probe_asserts_generated_text_not_its_derivation

import std.types { NonEmptyStr }
import gunbc.recurring_failure_mode { BelowCeiling, FoundBelowTheLadder, RecurringFailureMode, RungRead }
import gunbc.guarantee_rung { MechanicallyPreventable }
import gunbc.rung_climb { ClimbableButUnbuilt }
import std.decl_ref { DeclarationRef, WholeDeclaration }

// THREE SURVIVING RED CLAIMS were enrolled here, named by their actual causes, held until the repair
// owned by work item adhoc-972c2336-4c5 lands. STANDING CORRECTED 2026-10-27 (fierce-ferret-64, node
// adhoc-0201be55-56b): of the three, SURVIVING RED 3 (printer_and_main_workspace_modes_remain_dispatchable)
// is CLOSED -- it was measured GREEN on main, its stale spark_* roster had already been dropped by
// #15160, and it has now been re-expressed as a read of the closed roster, the mode-to-job assignment
// and the emitted job list, with its own RED and positive-control receipts below. TWO reds remain open
// (the two trusted_code_cannot_be_replaced_by_dispatch_revision probes), so this row stays BelowCeiling.
// The three are NOT regressions introduced by the re-contract of
// the three trusted-checkout claims (that re-contract turned test.claim.machine_intake.mtcollins1_boot_run_witness
// green, 39 -> 40 at the branch head); they are PRE-EXISTING reds measured identical at the branch
// base and at the branch head -- a control run at the base (dispatch ctl14, fresh build) and at the
// head (dispatch claimrun tables) report the same three failures on the same conjuncts, so nothing
// this PR does widens them, and the manager's side-chat ruling requires they carry a typed
// declaration naming their causes and a capability-based repair trigger rather than silence.

data a_dispatch_surface_probe_asserts_generated_text_not_its_derivation: RecurringFailureMode = RecurringFailureMode {
  identity: "a_dispatch_surface_probe_asserts_generated_text_not_its_derivation" as NonEmptyStr,

  rung: RungRead { found_at: FoundBelowTheLadder, standing: BelowCeiling { current: FoundBelowTheLadder, ceiling: MechanicallyPreventable, blocker: ClimbableButUnbuilt, trigger_capability: "the capability of re-expressing a fleet-converge dispatch-surface claim as a read of the mode-to-job assignment and the closed mode roster themselves -- the way gunbc.fleet.fleet_converge_workflow fleet_converge_shared_job_if already derives its selectors from fleet_converge_mode_job_id -- SUFFICIENT FOR the three named claims to keep their teeth across a re-derivation of the emitted if-condition or a mode retirement, and for a revert of that re-expression to turn them red again." } },

  receipts: [
    "**THE DEFECT:** a dispatch-surface probe asserts a literal substring of the EMITTED workflow text (an exclusion clause of the shared job's if-condition) or a literal roster of mode options, instead of reading the derivation those texts come from. When the derivation is legitimately re-shaped, the probe goes red on a true program. This is the same class gunbc.recurring_failure_mode.workflow_job_selection_diverges_from_mode_assignment closed for the shared job's own condition (#13607, 2026-10-09): the repair then MADE the shared job's if a positive derivation from fleet_converge_mode_job_id over the closed mode roster -- which is exactly what silently reddened the probes that kept asserting the retired NEGATIVE exclusion spelling.",
    "**SURVIVING RED 1, test.claim.namecheap_workflow_witness.trusted_code_cannot_be_replaced_by_dispatch_revision:** its fourth conjunct demands fleet_converge_shared_job_if contain \"github.event.inputs.mode != 'namecheap_observe'\". Since the #13607 re-derivation the shared job's if carries positive selectors only; namecheap_observe has its OWN dedicated job (emitted fleet-converge.yml: job 'namecheap_observe' with if github.event.inputs.mode == 'namecheap_observe'), so the negative clause the probe greps for no longer exists anywhere. The claim's first three conjuncts (the dispatch-revision ref expression, the event-sha arm, the absence of expected_revision) all hold. Cause: derivation re-shape (#13607 repair), not a lost security property.",
    "**SURVIVING RED 2, test.claim.printer_workflow_binding_witness.trusted_code_cannot_be_replaced_by_dispatch_revision:** identical shape -- its fourth conjunct demands fleet_converge_shared_job_if contain \"github.event.inputs.mode != 'printer'\"; printer likewise has its own dedicated emitted job (if github.event.inputs.mode == 'printer'), so the negative clause is gone. Its first three conjuncts hold.",
    "**SURVIVING RED 3, test.claim.printer_workflow_binding_witness.printer_and_main_workspace_modes_remain_dispatchable: CLOSED 2026-10-27 (node adhoc-0201be55-56b, fierce-ferret-64).** It demanded every one of eleven named modes appear exactly once in fleet_converge_mode_options. Four (printer, workspace_commissioning_plan, r2_workspace_object_read_mint, r2_workspace_object_write_mint) do; the seven spark_* names (spark_runtime_image_produce, spark_runtime_image_distribute, spark_arm_checkpoint_materialize, spark_arm_group_observe, spark_arm_group_launch_plan, spark_arm_group_launch, spark_arm_group_load) were REMOVED from FleetConvergeWorkflowMode by fa44b9810259 (2026-10-10, v1 closeout mega branch #13641) and their modes left the emitted options list. Cause: retired-mode roster, not a lost dispatch capability for the four surviving modes.",
    "**RED 3 IS NOT RED ON MAIN -- the standing was stale, measured 2026-10-27.** claim_batch --wet --functions at origin/main ae563700cbe (dispatch 2026-10-26 20:12 UTC, fresh build) prints PASS printer_and_main_workspace_modes_remain_dispatchable. The eleven-name roster was repaired by c62131787d3 (#15160, 2026-10-26, 'printer witness: drop the 7 modes #13641 retired from the dispatchable-modes list'), which is an ancestor of main; the four surviving names each appear exactly once in the 74-element fleet_converge_mode_options, which matches the emitted .github/workflows/fleet-converge.yml option list element for element. The guess that a lost excluded_from_dispatch filter caused it is FALSE on main: the filter is present at gunbc.fleet.fleet_converge_workflow:942 (filter(fleet_converge_workflow_modes, m => !fleet_converge_mode_is_spark_target_mode(mode: m))) and is LIVE -- the closed roster carries 81 modes, 7 of them spark_* (SparkGrants, SparkBootstrap, SparkServingApply, SparkNativeServingApply, SparkRuntimeImageProbe, SparkWirelessLinkConverge, SparkGrantsObserve), and the filter drops exactly those 7 to reach 74.",
    "**RED 3 CHAIN RE-DERIVATION (§6b): the CLAIM was stale, the product lost nothing -- but the claim was still this row's defect.** fa44b9810259's own message justifies the retirement ('every Spark sold... GitHub Actions rejects a workflow_dispatch input whose options list is empty, so the dead option goes with the fleet'), and no dag file anywhere still names the seven retired variants (grep over dag/: zero hits for each). So the eleven-name list was asserting retired modes, and #15160 corrected it. What remained unjustified is the SHAPE: it asserted a literal roster of wire names out of fleet_converge_mode_options, the generated input-choice projection, which is this row's own named defect. Repaired at that boundary: the witness now reads the closed roster in the mode's typed value (membership in fleet_converge_workflow_modes, non-exclusion by fleet_converge_spark_target_modes, exactly-once in the projection, and REACHABILITY through fleet_converge_mode_job_id into the emitted fleet_converge_jobs() list the yml is written from).",
    "**RED 3 RECEIPT (measured at the pushed head, claim_batch --wet --functions, one witness run per row).** GREEN at head: PASS printer_and_main_workspace_modes_remain_dispatchable + PASS spark_target_exclusion_filter_is_live (dispatch 2026-10-27 02:30 UTC). RED by re-introducing the defect in the PRODUCT, not the claim: (A) delete fleet_converge_printer_job() from fleet_converge_jobs() -- the mode stays listed and selectable but lands no job -- and the re-derived witness goes FAIL while the OLD projection-grep shape, run in the same dispatch, stays PASS (dispatch 2026-10-27 03:28 UTC): the projection cannot see a lost job, which is the row's defect demonstrated in one run. (B) list R2WorkspaceObjectWriteMint twice in fleet_converge_workflow_modes and the re-derived witness goes FAIL (roster 81 -> 82, options 74 -> 75) (dispatch 2026-10-27 03:48 UTC). POSITIVE CONTROL: spark_target_exclusion_filter_is_live passes at head and under both mutations, so the exclusion conjunct is not vacuous and the control is not collateral.",
    "**MEASURED, not inferred:** control dispatch ctl14 at branch base f4619452d9922c0ec9ce16a5ce8a2cce7470f09a (fresh build) reports namecheap 3/4 and printer 4/6 with exactly these failing names; the same run at the branch head reports the identical set, while mtcollins1_boot_run_witness moves 39/40 -> 40/40 (the re-contract's own RED -> GREEN). The three reds are therefore pre-existing main-side drift on other conjuncts, visible in the claim tables, un-enrolled before this row.",
    "**REPAIR OWNER:** work item adhoc-972c2336-4c5 (filed by the manager 2026-10-25). When the repair lands -- the three claims re-expressed as reads of fleet_converge_mode_job_id and the closed mode roster -- this row's trigger capability has fired and this row retires with it; the claims remain as ordinary regression controls.",
  ],
  evidence: [
    DeclarationRef { module_path: "test.claim.namecheap_workflow_witness", decl_name: "trusted_code_cannot_be_replaced_by_dispatch_revision", field: WholeDeclaration },
    DeclarationRef { module_path: "test.claim.printer_workflow_binding_witness", decl_name: "trusted_code_cannot_be_replaced_by_dispatch_revision", field: WholeDeclaration },
    DeclarationRef { module_path: "test.claim.printer_workflow_binding_witness", decl_name: "printer_and_main_workspace_modes_remain_dispatchable", field: WholeDeclaration },
    DeclarationRef { module_path: "gunbc.fleet.fleet_converge_workflow", decl_name: "fleet_converge_shared_job_if", field: WholeDeclaration },
    DeclarationRef { module_path: "gunbc.fleet.fleet_converge_workflow", decl_name: "fleet_converge_mode_job_id", field: WholeDeclaration },
  ],
}
